{"Title":"An Act relative to leaving the scene of a collision","BillNumber":"H1423","DocketNumber":"HD3345","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.02"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.02"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Timothy Cruz","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.0366667"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Timothy Shugrue","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.0533333"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Paul Tucker","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.0666667"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Michael Morrissey","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.0833333"},{"Id":null,"Name":"David Sullivan","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.1"},{"Id":null,"Name":"Joseph Early","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T00:54:29.1"},{"Id":"DFC1","Name":"Daniel Cahill","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DFC1","ResponseDate":"2023-04-04T16:42:07.2033333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1423/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Chan of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1423) of Tackey Chan and others relative to motor vehicle operators leaving the scene of a collision.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 24 of chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “property”, in line 932, the following words:- “or after having reason to know that he collided with or otherwise caused injury to any other vehicle or property,”. \r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 24 of said chapter 90, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by inserting after the words “death of any person”, in line 982, the following words:- “or after having reason to know that he collided with or otherwise caused injury to any person not resulting in the death of any person,”. \r\n\tSECTION 3. Section 24 of chapter 90, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out the word “shall”, in line 992, and inserting in place thereof the following words:- “or after having reason to know that he collided with or otherwise caused injury to any person, shall,”. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}